WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:09.048
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:15.031
Unit twenty: Academic Integrity. Today you will draw sharp contrasts with 'whereas'.

4
00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:17.762
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.759
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.617 --> 00:00:23.687
Integrity.

7
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:28.924
Integrity means consistent adherence to honest and ethical principles.

8
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:32.619
Integrity is tested most when no one is watching.

9
00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:35.823
Your turn. Say: Integrity.

10
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:39.749
Integrity.

11
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:41.438
Plagiarism.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.552
Plagiarism means passing off another's work as one's own.

13
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.206
AI tools have created new forms of plagiarism.

14
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:52.515
Your turn. Say: Plagiarism.

15
00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:56.379
Plagiarism.

16
00:00:57.117 --> 00:00:58.338
Attribution.

17
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.940
Attribution means acknowledging the source of an idea or text.

18
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.687
Attribution is required for data as well as words.

19
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:09.878
Your turn. Say: Attribution.

20
00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:13.897
Attribution.

21
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.756
Paraphrase.

22
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.118
Paraphrase means a restatement of a text in entirely new words and structure.

23
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.599
An accurate paraphrase still needs a citation.

24
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:28.021
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

25
00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:32.239
Paraphrase.

26
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:33.950
Honesty.

27
00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.844
Honesty means truthfulness in word and action.

28
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.262
Honesty about limitations strengthens a paper.

29
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.351
Your turn. Say: Honesty.

30
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.131
Honesty.

31
00:01:48.883 --> 00:01:50.024
Misconduct.

32
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:55.048
Misconduct means a serious breach of professional or ethical standards.

33
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.811
Data fabrication constitutes research misconduct.

34
00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:01.744
Your turn. Say: Misconduct.

35
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.915
Misconduct.

36
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:07.930
Originality.

37
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:12.994
Originality means the quality of being newly created by oneself.

38
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:16.558
Software now checks submissions for originality.

39
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.244
Your turn. Say: Originality.

40
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.322
Originality.

41
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:26.328
Accountability.

42
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:31.069
Accountability means being answerable for one's decisions and work.

43
00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:34.565
Accountability requires transparent methods.

44
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.429
Your turn. Say: Accountability.

45
00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:42.581
Accountability.

46
00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:46.797
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:54.203
Visal, some students say using AI to write an essay is no different from using a calculator. What's your view?

48
00:02:55.317 --> 00:03:03.844
I disagree. A calculator performs a process you understand, whereas an AI essay replaces the thinking itself.

49
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.809
But isn't plagiarism only about copying from people?

50
00:03:08.917 --> 00:03:19.838
Not really. Plagiarism undermines trust, whereas attribution builds it. Submitting unacknowledged AI text is still dishonest.

51
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.543
So should AI be banned?

52
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:31.527
No. Using it transparently for feedback seems acceptable, whereas hiding its use violates integrity.

53
00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.097
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.006
Grammar focus: Whereas for contrast.

55
00:03:38.306 --> 00:03:39.435
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.729
Plagiarism undermines trust, whereas attribution builds it.

57
00:03:44.617 --> 00:03:49.739
A calculator performs a process you understand, whereas an AI essay replaces the thinking.

58
00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:55.099
Whereas transparent use is acceptable, hidden use violates integrity.

59
00:03:56.033 --> 00:04:06.084
'Whereas' links two clauses that directly contrast two things. It is more formal than 'but' and can start the sentence. Don't use it for unexpected results; use 'although' for that.

60
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:13.334
Be careful! Don't say: Plagiarism destroys trust, whereas honesty destroys it too.

61
00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:19.401
Say: Plagiarism destroys trust, whereas honesty builds it.

62
00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:22.536
'Whereas' must introduce a real contrast.

63
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:25.904
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.967
Integrity in the Age of AI.

65
00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:35.806
Academic integrity has always rested on a simple principle: work submitted as your own must genuinely be yours.

66
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:43.118
Plagiarism undermines trust, whereas attribution builds it, by allowing readers to trace every idea to its source.

67
00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:50.696
Generative AI has complicated this principle, since text can now be produced without any identifiable human author.

68
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:59.017
Many universities now permit transparent use of AI for feedback, whereas undisclosed use is treated as misconduct.

69
00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:04.901
Ultimately, honesty and accountability matter more than any rule designed to enforce them.

70
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.153
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:11.017 --> 00:05:14.537
Plagiarism undermines trust, blank attribution builds it.

72
00:05:14.837 --> 00:05:18.850
A, whereas. B, although. C, despite.

73
00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.353
The answer is A: whereas.

74
00:05:25.517 --> 00:05:27.725
Which sentence uses 'whereas' correctly?

75
00:05:28.025 --> 00:05:35.893
A, Whereas it rained, we stayed home.. B, Cats are independent, whereas dogs are social.. C, He studied, whereas he passed..

76
00:05:39.433 --> 00:05:43.604
The answer is B: Cats are independent, whereas dogs are social..

77
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.504
Fabricating data constitutes research blank.

78
00:05:47.804 --> 00:05:51.887
A, attribution. B, misconduct. C, originality.

79
00:05:55.433 --> 00:05:57.468
The answer is B: misconduct.

80
00:05:58.617 --> 00:06:02.497
For an unexpected contrast ('she was tired but kept working'), use blank.

81
00:06:02.797 --> 00:06:06.532
A, whereas. B, although. C, thereby.

82
00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.788
The answer is B: although.

83
00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:17.411
According to the reading, how do many universities treat undisclosed AI use?

84
00:06:17.711 --> 00:06:22.525
A, as misconduct. B, as acceptable feedback. C, as a calculator.

85
00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.275
The answer is A: as misconduct.

86
00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:32.641
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:33.483 --> 00:06:36.981
Why does academic integrity matter beyond avoiding punishment?

88
00:06:53.783 --> 00:06:55.260
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:31.367
Academic integrity matters because the purpose of education is to develop your own abilities, not just to obtain a certificate. A student who copies may pass the course, whereas a student who struggles honestly actually learns. Furthermore, society relies on qualifications: we trust that a doctor or engineer genuinely earned their degree. Some may argue that dishonesty is harmless if no one finds out. However, every shortcut weakens both your skills and public trust.

90
00:07:31.667 --> 00:07:33.794
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:34.683 --> 00:07:39.054
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and whereas for contrast.

92
00:07:39.354 --> 00:07:42.831
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

93
00:07:43.131 --> 00:07:45.899
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:49.571
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

